-- =============================================================================
-- Migration: model_training_priority_governance_expansion
-- =============================================================================
--
-- Purpose
--   Expand the control plane for (1) model-training consent and eligibility,
--   (2) provider priority / queue semantics during peak load, and (3) org-level
--   governance, audit, and operational telemetry. This migration is additive:
--   new columns are nullable or carry safe defaults so existing application
--   reads and writes continue to work without a coordinated deploy.
--
-- Scope (high level)
--   • Training opt-in: profile defaults, per-user settings, workspace policy,
--     append-only consent events, and training flags on usage/memory rows.
--   • Priority queues: plan/subscription snapshots, rate-limit queue fields,
--     router rules, runtime priority snapshots, capacity windows, Nomita routing.
--   • Governance: compliance tiers, DPA/legal-hold, data classification, audit
--     enrichment, moderation training blocks, feature-flag rollout metadata.
--   • New tables: model_training_consent_events, model_usage_realtime_windows,
--     model_priority_runtime_snapshots, provider_capacity_windows.
--   • RLS + grants: user-readable consent/snapshots; internal ops tables locked
--     down; service_role and optional dashboard/read-only role grants.
--
-- Dependencies
--   Assumes core platform tables from earlier migrations (profiles, workspaces,
--   plans, subscriptions, model_catalog, model_router_rules, etc.).
--
-- Rollout notes
--   • Plan priority semantics are seeded at the end; re-run safe via UPDATE … WHERE.
--   • Realtime publication for model_usage_realtime_windows is best-effort (duplicate
--     publication errors are swallowed).
--   • Ends with `-- omitted on CRDB: NOTIFY pgrst (PostgREST)


